{"is_source_file": true, "format": "shell script", "description": "This file contains a shell script that defines an alias for executing remote commands (R), manipulates firewall and NAT settings on a device for enabling and verifying MASQUERADE rules in iptables, and restores previous states upon cleanup. It is used for configuration management and verification related to network address translation (NAT) rules.", "external_files": ["firewall", "/etc/init.d/firewall", "iptables"], "external_methods": ["uci", "iptables-save", "grep", "sed", "sleep"], "published": [], "classes": [], "methods": [], "calls": ["uci -q show firewall", "awk -F\"[=\\\\[\\\\]]\"", "uci -q get firewall.@zone[$WAN_IDX]", "uci -q set firewall.@zone[$WAN_IDX].masq=1", "uci -q commit firewall", "/etc/init.d/firewall reload", "iptables-save -t nat", "grep -E \"^-A POSTROUTING\"", "grep -E \"\\\\bMASQUERADE\\\\b\"", "sed \"s/[[:space:]]\\\\+/ /g\"", "/etc/init.d/firewall reload"], "search-terms": ["iptables", "MASQUERADE", "firewall", "WAN zone", "NAT", "masquerade rule", "ukci commands", "postrouting verification"], "state": 2, "file_id": 24, "knowledge_revision": 83, "git_revision": "c0b8af75b65e217bf82efe3ba5d6f2941675830f", "hash": "1e801c5d77933e517fbc0127984ed30a", "format-version": 4, "code-base-name": "cram_sample-3556", "filename": "sample_case/iptables/18-iptables-nat-masquerade.t", "revision_history": [{"83": "c0b8af75b65e217bf82efe3ba5d6f2941675830f"}]}